  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$ \n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n\nI. $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ if and only if $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$\n\nII. If $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ then $x\\in {Z}^{-},$ or if $x\\in {Z}^{-}$ then $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}.$\n\nIII. $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ is equivalent to  $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$",
